IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch2-reduction-periods`

-- Schedule 11 to the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376): application of ESA or JSA sanctions to universal credit.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- The Schedule has effect by regulation 112 (see uc4-part8-ch2-miscellaneous.l4). This text carries no made or commencement date.
-- What days "apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations" or under "regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's
-- Allowance Regulations 2013" is not in the inputs: the rules take the number of days as a stated input.

§ `Schedule 11 — Application of ESA or JSA sanctions to universal credit`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 1 — Moving an ESA sanction to UC`

-- Paragraph 1(1): applies where (a) a person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance; (b) there is a reduction
-- relating to the award under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007; and (c) the person becomes entitled to universal credit.
-- out of range: section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 (not among the inputs): whether a reduction relates to the award is a stated input
-- src:2873 | SCHEDULE 11 — Application of ESA or JSA sanctions to universal credit
-- src:2874 | 1 Moving an ESA sanction to UC
-- src:2875 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2876 | (a) a person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance;
-- src:2877 | (b) there is a reduction relating to the award of the employment and support allowance under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 ; and
-- src:2878 | (c) the person becomes entitled to universal credit.
@ref Sch 11 para 1(1) (src:2873-2878)
GIVEN `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a reduction relating to the award of the employment and support allowance under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 11 para 1(1) — this paragraph applies` `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance` `there is a reduction relating to the award of the employment and support allowance under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007` `the person becomes entitled to universal credit` MEANS
    `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to an employment and support allowance`
    AND `there is a reduction relating to the award of the employment and support allowance under section 11J of the Welfare Reform Act 2007`
    AND `the person becomes entitled to universal credit`

-- Paragraph 1(2): any reduction relating to the ESA award is to be applied to the award of universal credit.
-- src:2879 | (2) Any reduction relating to the award of the employment and support allowance is to be applied to the award of universal credit.
@ref Sch 11 para 1(2) (src:2879)
GIVEN `this paragraph applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 11 para 1(2) — the reduction is applied to the award of universal credit` `this paragraph applies` MEANS
    `this paragraph applies`

-- Paragraph 1(3): the period is the number of days that apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations, minus (a) any
-- days that have already resulted in a reduction of the ESA and (b) if the ESA award has terminated, the days after the date of termination
-- and before the day the award of universal credit starts; and the period is added to the total outstanding reduction period. A period
-- is not made less than nought (fork F-sch11-1). Days "after" termination and "before" the start are the days strictly between.
-- out of range: regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations (not among the inputs): the number of days is a stated input
-- src:2880 | (3) The period for which the reduction is to have effect is the number of days which apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations minus—
-- src:2881 | (a) any days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the employment and support allowance; and
-- src:2882 | (b) if the award of the employment and support allowance has terminated, any days falling after the date of that termination and before the date on which the award of universal credits starts,
-- src:2883 | and that period is to be added to the total outstanding reduction period.
@ref Sch 11 para 1(3) (src:2880-2883)
GIVEN `number of days which apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations` IS A NUMBER
      `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the employment and support allowance` IS A NUMBER
      `date on which the award of the employment and support allowance terminated` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the award of universal credit starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 para 1(3) — the period for which the reduction is to have effect` `number of days which apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations` `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the employment and support allowance` `date on which the award of the employment and support allowance terminated` `date on which the award of universal credit starts` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, (`number of days which apply to the person under regulations 52 and 53 of the ESA Regulations` MINUS `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the employment and support allowance`) MINUS `days between termination and the start`)
    WHERE
        `days between termination and the start` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date on which the award of the employment and support allowance terminated`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST ended THEN maximum (LIST 0, (Day `date on which the award of universal credit starts` MINUS Day ended) MINUS 1)

@ref Sch 11 para 1(3) (src:2883)
GIVEN `total outstanding reduction period before` IS A NUMBER
      `period for which the reduction is to have effect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 para 1(3) — the total outstanding reduction period once the period is added` `total outstanding reduction period before` `period for which the reduction is to have effect` MEANS
    `total outstanding reduction period before` PLUS `period for which the reduction is to have effect`

-- Paragraph 1(4): the amount of the reduction for an assessment period is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110
-- (coverage row: inert, a pure citation; the rule for regulation 110 is in uc4-part8-ch2-reduction-effect.l4).
-- src:2884 | (4) The amount of the reduction in the award of universal credit for any assessment period in which the reduction is applied is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110.
@ref Sch 11 para 1(4) (src:2884)
`Sch 11 para 1(4) — the amount of the reduction is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110` MEANS
        "The amount of the reduction in the award of universal credit for any assessment period in which the reduction is applied is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 2 — Moving a JSA sanction to UC`

-- Paragraph 2(1): applies where (a) a person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance; (b) there is a reduction relating to
-- the award under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995; and (c) the person becomes entitled to universal credit.
-- out of range: sections 6J and 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (not among the inputs): whether a reduction relates to the award is a stated input
-- src:2885 | 2 Moving a JSA sanction to UC
-- src:2886 | (1) This paragraph applies where—
-- src:2887 | (a) a person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance;
-- src:2888 | (b) there is a reduction relating to the person's award of a jobseeker's allowance under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995 ; and
-- src:2889 | (c) the person becomes entitled to universal credit.
@ref Sch 11 para 2(1) (src:2885-2889)
GIVEN `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a reduction relating to the person's award of a jobseeker's allowance under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes entitled to universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 11 para 2(1) — this paragraph applies` `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` `there is a reduction relating to the person's award of a jobseeker's allowance under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995` `the person becomes entitled to universal credit` MEANS
    `the person is, or has ceased to be, entitled to a jobseeker's allowance`
    AND `there is a reduction relating to the person's award of a jobseeker's allowance under section 6J or 6K of the Jobseekers Act 1995`
    AND `the person becomes entitled to universal credit`

-- Paragraph 2(2): any reduction relating to the JSA award is to be applied to the award of universal credit.
-- src:2890 | (2) Any reduction relating to the award of the jobseeker's allowance is to be applied to the award of universal credit.
@ref Sch 11 para 2(2) (src:2890)
GIVEN `this paragraph applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 11 para 2(2) — the reduction is applied to the award of universal credit` `this paragraph applies` MEANS
    `this paragraph applies`

-- Paragraph 2(3): the period is the number of days that apply under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013, minus
-- (a) days already resulted in a reduction of the JSA and (b) if the JSA award has terminated, the days after the date of termination and
-- before the day the award of universal credit starts; and the period is added to the total outstanding reduction period.
-- out of range: regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013 (not among the inputs): the number of days is a stated input
-- src:2891 | (3) The period for which the reduction is to have effect is the number of days which apply to the person under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013 minus—
-- src:2892 | (a) any days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the jobseeker's allowance; and
-- src:2893 | (b) if the award of the jobseeker's allowance has terminated, any days falling after the date of that termination and before the date on which the award of universal credits starts,
-- src:2894 | and that period is to be added to the total outstanding reduction period.
@ref Sch 11 para 2(3) (src:2891-2894)
GIVEN `number of days which apply to the person under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013` IS A NUMBER
      `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the jobseeker's allowance` IS A NUMBER
      `date on which the award of the jobseeker's allowance terminated` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the award of universal credit starts` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 para 2(3) — the period for which the reduction is to have effect` `number of days which apply to the person under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013` `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the jobseeker's allowance` `date on which the award of the jobseeker's allowance terminated` `date on which the award of universal credit starts` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, (`number of days which apply to the person under regulations 19 to 21 of the Jobseeker's Allowance Regulations 2013` MINUS `days which have already resulted in a reduction to the amount of the jobseeker's allowance`) MINUS `days between termination and the start`)
    WHERE
        `days between termination and the start` MEANS
            CONSIDER `date on which the award of the jobseeker's allowance terminated`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 0
            WHEN JUST ended THEN maximum (LIST 0, (Day `date on which the award of universal credit starts` MINUS Day ended) MINUS 1)

@ref Sch 11 para 2(3) (src:2894)
GIVEN `total outstanding reduction period before` IS A NUMBER
      `period for which the reduction is to have effect` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Sch 11 para 2(3) — the total outstanding reduction period once the period is added` `total outstanding reduction period before` `period for which the reduction is to have effect` MEANS
    `total outstanding reduction period before` PLUS `period for which the reduction is to have effect`

-- Paragraph 2(4): the amount of the reduction for an assessment period is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110
-- (coverage row: inert, a pure citation).
-- src:2895 | (4) The amount of the reduction in the award of universal credit for any assessment period in which the reduction is applied is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110.
@ref Sch 11 para 2(4) (src:2895)
`Sch 11 para 2(4) — the amount of the reduction is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110` MEANS
        "The amount of the reduction in the award of universal credit for any assessment period in which the reduction is applied is the amount calculated in accordance with regulation 110."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 3 — Effect of ESA or JSA sanction on escalation of UC sanction`

-- Paragraph 3: where (a) a reduction for an ESA or JSA award is applied to an award of universal credit under paragraph 1 or 2, (b) there is a
-- subsequent sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27, and (c) the failure giving rise to the earlier reduction and its reduction period
-- correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 to which the same period would apply under Chapter 2 of Part 8, then for the
-- purposes of the reduction period for the subsequent failure the previous failure is treated as if it were the corresponding failure.
-- The result is the previous failure as the Chapter 2 rules read it (with the flags of the corresponding failure), or NOTHING when the
-- paragraph does not apply. Which failure corresponds, and the flags that follow, are for the caller to say.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
-- src:2896 | 3 Effect of ESA or JSA sanction on escalation of UC sanction
-- src:2897 | Where—
-- src:2898 | (a) a reduction in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance or an award of a jobseeker's allowance is applied to an award of universal credit by virtue of paragraph 1 or 2;
-- src:2899 | (b) there is a subsequent sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act; and
-- src:2900 | (c) the failure giving rise to the reduction in relation to the award of an employment and support allowance or the award of a jobseeker's allowance (“the previous failure”) and the reduction period determined for that failure correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 of the Act to which the same reduction period would apply under Chapter 2 of Part 8 of these Regulations,
-- src:2901 | for the purposes of determining the reduction period for that subsequent failure, the previous failure is to be treated as if it were the corresponding failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
@ref Sch 11 para 3 (src:2896-2901)
GIVEN `a reduction in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance or of a jobseeker's allowance is applied to an award of universal credit by virtue of paragraph 1 or 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a subsequent sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the previous failure and the reduction period determined for it correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 of the Act to which the same reduction period would apply under Chapter 2 of Part 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the previous failure treated as the corresponding failure` IS A `Previous sanctionable failure`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Previous sanctionable failure`
`Sch 11 para 3 — the previous failure is treated as the corresponding failure` `a reduction in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance or of a jobseeker's allowance is applied to an award of universal credit by virtue of paragraph 1 or 2` `there is a subsequent sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act` `the previous failure and the reduction period determined for it correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 of the Act to which the same reduction period would apply under Chapter 2 of Part 8` `the previous failure treated as the corresponding failure` MEANS
    IF `a reduction in relation to an award of an employment and support allowance or of a jobseeker's allowance is applied to an award of universal credit by virtue of paragraph 1 or 2`
       AND `there is a subsequent sanctionable failure under section 26 or 27 of the Act`
       AND `the previous failure and the reduction period determined for it correspond with a failure specified under section 26 or 27 of the Act to which the same reduction period would apply under Chapter 2 of Part 8`
    THEN JUST `the previous failure treated as the corresponding failure`
    ELSE NOTHING
